                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is a fast-paced arcade puzzle game, which I feel has gone from a staple of Japanese gaming to an underrepresented genre. \n\nIt is very, very mechanically similar to Puyo Puyo. But it's got two big differences. The first is that you only need to match 3 same-colour things together, instead of 4. The second is there's a meter you can build up and if you push both left & right rotation buttons simultaneously, it does a special move, to remove grey blocks and counter your opponent. There's also a minor difference in that you don't get a bonus attack for completely clearing the blocks on your screen.\n\nRegarding difficulty: \n\nI guess it all comes down to how naturally making chains is to you. I found that the 3-block match and there only being a few different colours on the board means that it's actually perhaps too easy to make a match, and you're constantly trying to think in terms of not screwing up the chains you're constructing, which means I was really taking a different approach. However, I also think: \"Very Easy\" and \"Easy\" modes are maybe too easy. \"Normal\" mode... I played for 45 minutes and just was stuck on the first battle. Not in danger of losing, but hardly about to win either. \"Hard\" seemed like a better difficulty to play at, as it's more like - strike at the right moment and wait for your opponent to screw up.\n\nPros:\n\n* It's pretty much Puyo Puyo\n* It's cheap\n* It's accesible to colourblind people - the different colours are different shapes.\n* Responsive controls, doesn't feel laggy\n* Full controller support right out of the box\n\nCons: \n\n* The story mode translation quality is awful.\n* It doesn't seem to have much of a story anyway\n* Difficulty balance is iffy\n* There's no full clear bonus or anything\n* The interface feels just as cheap as it is. If you pause the game, there's not even a pause menu.\n\nOther points that could be pro or con depending on your interpretation:\n\n* It contains characters from \"Happiness!\"\n* Pleasant, upbeat, cheerful music. \n\nOverall, I'm giving this game a thumbs up.\n\nBut I'd also suggest - if you can pay a bit more and get Puyo Puyo Tetris, you'll probably be much happier with it.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1526743111,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1526743214,
                        "voted_up": true,
